= The Death of Kornilov

Paul von Hindenburg has passed away at age 64 from tubercolosis. He had reportedly contracted the disease while visiting Ukraine, this does explain his unusual absence since he left office.

The nation engages in an outpouring of grief for its war hero and former president. Even for committed socialists and republicans, this is a bittersweet moment. Even though he was a manifestation of Russian militarism and Conservatism, he still led the nation through difficult times, without destroying democracy. It could always have been worse.

With the passing of Kornilov, it seems as if an era of history is closing. The worst years of crisis are over, and nationalism's days are numbered. Perhaps Russia will finally enter into a new era of genuine peace...
